  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "10.7.0 - Breaking: the AntD-style calendar-dropdown date control, formerly EditDatePicker<T>, is renamed to EditDate<T> and is now the default date control -- the previous native-input EditDate<T> is renamed to EditDateNative<T>. A compile-time-obsolete EditDatePicker<T> stub catches stale `<EditDatePicker>` markup with a build error, but a bare existing `<EditDate>` reference that meant the native input still compiles -- it silently renders the calendar dropdown instead; audit every EditDate usage before upgrading and switch to EditDateNative if you need the old native-input behavior. The new EditDate also needs wss-controls.css and the lazily-imported wss-picker.js (previously only edit-controls.css), so an app linking just edit-controls.css now renders an unstyled date field with no dropdown. New (Edit Controls): EditDate<T> gains Size (SelectSize, wss-picker-sm/lg) and ParsingErrorMessage (default \"The {0} field must be a date.\", surfaced via its own ValidationMessageStore when typed text isn't a date at all) -- both added to the picker before the rename above, so EditDate is a genuine superset of the old EditDatePicker, not a regression; EditDate deliberately has no UpdateOn (a picker commits on selection/parse, not per keystroke -- use EditDateNative for that axis); UpdateTrigger enum + UpdateOn parameter (plus FormDefaults.UpdateOn) to choose commit-on-keystroke vs. commit-on-blur/Enter for EditString/EditTextArea/EditNumber/EditDateNative/the Radio \"Other\" box; [Placeholder(\"...\")] model attribute (with [Display(Prompt)] fallback) honored by EditString/EditTextArea/EditNumber/EditDate/EditDateRange/EditSelectSearch/EditMultiSelect/EditSelectEnum/EditSelectString. New (UI Kit): DatePicker/DateRangePicker gain Size (SelectSize, wss-picker-sm/lg), the same parameter EditDate forwards; Select.AriaErrorMessage, forwarded by EditSelectSearch/EditMultiSelect, plus aria-errormessage on EditFile. Changed: default checkbox/radio label spacing now matches AntD's 8px flex-row gap for every EditBool/EditCheckedStringList/EditCheckedEnumList/EditRadioString/EditRadioEnum/EditRadio label, not just the UseStyledCheckbox variant -- a visible default-rendering change for every consumer; EditSelectSearch.Placeholder/EditMultiSelect.Placeholder are now string? (previously string, defaulted to \"Please select\"). Fixed: the new flex checkbox/radio labels are hardened against a consumer's own input flex/margin resets; EditSelectEnum ports EditSelectString's no-JS selected-option fallback for prerender/no-JS rendering; the Select engine's value-to-label lookup is unified across Select/EditSelectSearch/EditMultiSelect, fixing label drift on a duplicate-valued option list; SearchInput's clear/search buttons no longer collapse under a consumer's button height reset; the JS overlay positioning helpers are consolidated, fixing inconsistent dropdown/panel flip-to-fit behavior. Internal refactors (shared bases/components, CSS/JS/icon dedup, hoisted e2e scaffolding) and dependency/test-infra bumps (ASP.NET Core Components, bUnit, Playwright) with no consumer-facing API change. See the README changelog for details.",
